module gunbc.p3a1_self_fork_homonym_disposition

data p3a1_bit_homonym_hold_note: String = "P3a-1 HOLD (parent rulings msg_41dbc4b4, msg_766977de): the Bit census row is a measurement artifact, not a production co-resolution defect. The failing diagnostic is fixture-vs-fixture — synthetic.parse_mechanism.nest_d1..nest_d4 each declare 'type Bit = B0 | B1' in four independent modules that never co-resolve in any real compilation; they collide only inside the forced whole-corpus synthetic closure. The diagnostic fires on the VARIANT names (B0, B1), not the type name: renaming all four to one shared MechanismBit leaves 'variant B0 appears in both MechanismBit and MechanismBit' — B0 and B1 untouched, collision verbatim. Four distinct type names would change the outcome but is churn against a measurement artifact. Under namespace-only resolution qualified names differ (nest_d1.Bit vs nest_d2.Bit, etc.) and the collision dissolves for free. No rename."

data p3a1_condition_homonym_hold_note: String = "P3a-1 HOLD (parent rulings msg_41dbc4b4, msg_766977de): examples.interp_test.Condition and examples.weather.Condition are independent example modules that never import each other. They are ambiguous only inside the forced whole-corpus synthetic closure; qualified names differ under namespace-only end state. Distinct renames (InterpCondition/WeatherCondition) would technically clear it but are the same artifact class — churn against a census number that is not real. No rename."

data p3a1_production_homonym_caveat_note: String = "P3a-1 caveat (parent ruling msg_41dbc4b4): the whole-corpus census cannot prove any production pair is genuinely co-resolved in a real closure — the synthetic root forces everything together. The authoritative ambiguity population comes from the compiler fold over real closures. KeySource, JsonValue, and YamlValue renames in this lane are safe because they are live production carriers with verified overlapping consumers, not because the census count alone established co-resolution."

data p3a1_variant_vs_type_homonym_note: String = "P3a-1 scope boundary (review 45577): the Bit hold note cites variant-level VariantCollision because four fixtures share one type name Bit — renaming the type without renaming B0/B1 is ineffective. JsonValue/YamlValue/KeySource census rows were duplicate unqualified TYPE declarations across dag/ and src/v2/ forks, not shared variant arms in one module. After the outer-type rename, shared variant spellings (JsonNull, PathParam, etc.) are a separate per-module constructor-namespace question: VariantCollision fires only when one module's flat namespace (locals plus direct imports) binds the same arm name to two owners. Corpus grep finds zero modules that directly import both extdeps.languages.json.emit and v2.extdeps.formats.json (or both yaml.types and v2.extdeps.formats.yaml); v2.std.effects imports std.effects without KeySource/PathParam/InputField. v2 consumers reference JsonSchemaCarrierValue/YamlSchemaCarrierValue as field types only — no bare JsonNull/YamlNull construction sites. Distinct variant modeling or full carrier unification remains the format-design lane, not this homonym-rename lane."
